      {
        "y": 12.7,
        "x0": 33.2,
        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "35"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 420.4,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Authorities: customs and police"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 202,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Entering a country"
      },
      {
        "y": 96.9,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 500.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "On arrival in most countries, you have to show your passport or national identity card, possibly a landing"
      },
      {
        "y": 107.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 476.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "card1 and often a customs declaration form2. You may need a visa and a vaccination certificate3,"
      },
      {
        "y": 118.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 494.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "depending on entry regulations4. Alternatively, some passengers can use e-passport gates which make"
      },
      {
        "y": 129.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 491.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "use of facial recognition technology5. Customs officers carry out spot checks6 on people’s baggage to"
      },
      {
        "y": 140.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 490.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "find banned or restricted goods7 and to check that you haven’t gone over your allowance8. They may"
      },
      {
        "y": 151.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 504.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "use sniffer/detector dogs9 to detect10 drugs, tobacco, cash or explosives. In most cases, you have to clear"
      },
      {
        "y": 162.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 492.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "customs11 at the port of entry12. Some passengers may wish to be recognised as refugees13 and claim"
      },
      {
        "y": 173.1,
        "x0": 107.2,
        "x1": 431.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "asylum14. People who claim asylum in this way are sometimes called asylum-seekers."
      },
      {
        "y": 198.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 form with your personal details and date of arrival 2 form showing how much money and what goods you"
      },
      {
        "y": 210.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are carrying 3 paper proving you have had the necessary health injections 4 rules about who can enter"
      },
      {
        "y": 222.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a country and for how long 5 computer application that can automatically identify a person from a visual"
      },
      {
        "y": 234.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "image 6 checks done as a sample, rather than checking everyone or everything 7 items that are forbidden"
      },
      {
        "y": 246.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "or only permitted in specified quantities 8 amount permitted by law 9 specially trained dogs who locate"
      },
      {
        "y": 258.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "specific items using their sense of smell 10 find something hidden 11 successfully get through baggage"
      },
      {
        "y": 270.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 500,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "checking 12 the port or airport where you first enter a country 13 people who have escaped from their"
      },
      {
        "y": 282.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "own country for political reasons 14 /əˈsaɪləm/ to request permission to stay in another country to avoid"
      },
      {
        "y": 295.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 419.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "persecution back home [cruel treatment because of race, religion or political beliefs]"
      },
      {
        "y": 315.9,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 206,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Policing the streets"
      },
      {
        "y": 333.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 290.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The police enforce the law. [make people obey]"
      },
      {
        "y": 345.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 377.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A police officer can stop and search you if there is a suspicion you"
      },
      {
        "y": 357.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 383.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are carrying drugs, weapons or stolen property. [belief that something"
      },
      {
        "y": 370.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 162.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "may be the case]"
      },
      {
        "y": 381.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 370.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The police cannot normally enter your home against your wishes"
      },
      {
        "y": 393.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 387,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "without a search warrant. [official permission from a judge or magistrate"
      },
      {
        "y": 406.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 166.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to search a home]"
      },
      {
        "y": 417.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 368.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Many roads have safety/speed cameras to ensure people aren’t"
      },
      {
        "y": 429.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 364.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "exceeding the speed limit. [going faster than the permitted speed]"
      },
      {
        "y": 441.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 382.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Traffic wardens issue parking tickets, with fines for illegal parking."
      },
      {
        "y": 454.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 380.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[people whose job it is to make sure drivers do not leave their cars where it"
      },
      {
        "y": 466.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 154.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is not allowed]"
      },
      {
        "y": 477.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The police also use surveillance /səˈveɪləns/ techniques, including CCTV (closed-circuit television)"
      },
      {
        "y": 489.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to monitor public areas such as town centres and airports. [television system sending signals to a limited"
      },
      {
        "y": 502.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 171.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "number of screens]"
      },
      {
        "y": 522.8,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 225.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Other types of policing"
      },
      {
        "y": 540.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 397.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "security forces: often a name for the army and police working together"
      },
      {
        "y": 552.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 324.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "plain-clothes police: police who do not wear uniform"
      },
      {
        "y": 564.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 405.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "undercover police: police who are working secretly, using a false identity"
      },
      {
        "y": 576.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 372.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "drug squad: police specially trained to fight the illegal drug trade"
      },
      {
        "y": 588.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "anti-corruption squad: police specially trained to discover and fight bribery/corruption [dishonest"
      },
      {
        "y": 601.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 344.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "behaviour usually involving using money illegally to gain favours]"
      },
      {
        "y": 612.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "cybercrime: computer crime (there are many types, including cyberterrorism, cyberwarfare,"
      },
      {
        "y": 624.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 484.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "phishing = tricking people on the internet to give up personal information, particularly bank"
      },
      {
        "y": 636.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 165.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "account details)"
      },
      {
        "y": 660.1,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 219.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Common mistakes"
      },
      {
        "y": 684,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 350.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Police is a plural word: The police are trying to combat crime."
      }
    ],
