        "tag": "main",
        "text": "35.1"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 497.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Rewrite these sentences using phrases and collocations from A opposite instead of the"
      },
      {
        "y": 83.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 197.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "underlined words."
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 535.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 You’ll have to show a paper proving that you have had injections for infectious diseases when you"
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 202.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "enter the country."
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 501.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 People entering from war-torn countries often ask for permission to stay to avoid political"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 263.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "oppression in their own country."
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 515.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 You have to take your baggage through customs if you arrive on an international flight at San"
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 368.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Francisco airport, even if you are flying on within the USA."
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 524.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 You may have to fill in a paper saying how much money you’re bringing into the country before"
      },
      {
        "y": 184,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 258.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "going through customs control."
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 531.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 At the airport now, they use a system that checks that the photo in the passport is actually of the"
      },
      {
        "y": 208,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 238.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "person using the passport."
      },
      {
        "y": 220,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 508.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 Passenger to airline cabin attendant: Could you give me one of those papers for filling in my"
      },
      {
        "y": 232,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 393.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "passport number and personal details before we arrive, please?"
      },
      {
        "y": 244,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 456.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 At the airport, the security guards had those special dogs that can smell drugs."
      },
      {
        "y": 256,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 442.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 You’ll need a visa; the rules about who can enter the country are very strict."
      },
      {
        "y": 268,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 450.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "9 You have to fill in the city where you first entered the country in this box here."
      },
      {
        "y": 284.3,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "35.2"
      },
      {
        "y": 286.9,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 283.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Match the words to form collocations."
      },
      {
        "y": 303.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 455.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 detector 6 spot a squad f ticket"
      },
      {
